From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 00:05:46 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] localspl, winspool: a CUPS printer's queue is the printer's: its documents are listed, paused and cancelled (9812)

Wine's spooler runs in the program that prints, and a job ends when the
CUPS port has handed the data to CUPS: the document then waits in CUPS's
queue, where no Windows program could see it. EnumJobs from any other
process (a queue window, Settings, a program watching its document) was
always empty, PRINTER_INFO_2's cJobs was 0, SetJob found no job to pause
or cancel, and SetPrinter's pause set a registry flag nothing read -- a
jammed printer's stuck document could not be cancelled from Windows.

A CUPS printer's queue is now CUPS's, as a network printer's queue is its
server's on Windows:
- localspl: EnumJobs and GetJob list the CUPS queue's not-completed jobs
  after the ones being spooled here (IPP Get-Jobs as the user: name,
  owner, state, size, pages, priority, time submitted; another user's
  document keeps CUPS's privacy). SetJob's pause, resume, restart and
  cancel are IPP Hold-Job, Release-Job, Restart-Job and Cancel-Job, which
  CUPS allows the document's owner and administrators. A new fpSetPrinter
  pauses, resumes and purges the CUPS queue (IPP Pause-Printer,
  Resume-Printer, Purge-Jobs: administrators, as CUPS decides).
- winspool: SetPrinter's commands go to the provider first (other printers
  keep the registry flag); cJobs counts the queue's documents (one
  cupsGetJobs2 in the two-second status cache).
- A Windows program has no terminal for CUPS to ask a password at: the
  calling thread's password callback answers none (access denied).
- The document title given to CUPS was converted into len + 3 + 1 bytes
  instead of len * 3 + 1, so a title with accented or CJK characters was
  cut short in CUPS's queue.

Gate test/cupsjobs-gate.sh (a CUPS server of its own).

